WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.187 --> 00:00:02.770
(upbeat piano)

00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:21.995
- [Narrator] 30 miles northwest of Seoul,

00:00:21.995 --> 00:00:25.919
there is a city in Korea
dedicated to all things books.

00:00:25.919 --> 00:00:28.229
And this gentleman has been
working to save a piece

00:00:28.229 --> 00:00:31.146
of the country's printing heritage.

00:00:48.855 --> 00:00:50.520
- [Narrator] Okay, so
letterpress printing is when you

00:00:50.520 --> 00:00:53.770
push raised metal types into the paper.

00:00:56.664 --> 00:01:00.164
- [Narrator] And how does it work exactly?

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:33.265
- [Narrator] And Korea
actually has a long history

00:01:33.265 --> 00:01:34.873
of developing printing techniques,

00:01:34.873 --> 00:01:37.300
including the letterpress,
which is usually credited

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.335
to Johannes Gutenberg of Germany

00:01:39.335 --> 00:01:42.168
who introduced printing to Europe.

00:01:54.258 --> 00:01:56.130
- [Narrator] However, in
the ’80's, a new technology,

00:01:56.130 --> 00:02:00.297
offset printing, took over
as the industry standard.

00:02:10.947 --> 00:02:12.545
And while letterpress may not make sense for

00:02:12.545 --> 00:02:14.511
most printing today, Park has found those

00:02:14.511 --> 00:02:17.594
who appreciate it as much as he does.

00:02:30.908 --> 00:02:33.491
(upbeat music)

